    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not retire the 30 AxReal axioms, and `nat_axiom_inventory` still reports real: axiom=30. Satisfiable by a constructed object is not the same as unnecessary: 57 files name the AxReal symbols, 13 are rewrite-required consumers, LraReconstructCtx and the ordered-ring telescope touch all 30 fields across 158 accesses, and the axiom ledger is 30 of 30 real. Retiring them is a migration, not a deletion. What it DOES discharge is ADR-0456's caveat that the only model was Int -- 'Int is not R' was the honest limit of that relative-consistency result and no longer applies. Nor is Eq CReal on offer as real equality; it is CReal.Equiv, and the nine restated laws say so in their own statements.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
